(13) Digital certificate : electronic record secured by the electronic signa ture of the person 
who issued it after ensuring that it certifies the authenticity of its contents;

(14) Qualified electronic certificate : digital certificate issued by a licensed Certific ation 
Authority;

(15) Electronic certification : issuance of electronic certificates;

(16) Cipher : the transformation of information using a secret key to make it illegible to 
anyone except those possessing special knowledge of the key;

(17) Key : in a cipher system, it corresponds to a mathemati cal value, a word, or a phrase 
which enables the ciphering or deciphering of a mes sage with the help of the encryption 
algorithm;

(18) Private key : key used in asymmetric cipher mechanism (or publi c key cipher) which 
belongs to an entity and kept secret;

(19) Public key : used to cipher a message in an asymmetric system distributed freely;

